  "takeaways": [
    "Past p = n test error descends again while training error stays at zero.",
    "In 20-D random features the second descent beats the classical sweet spot; in 1-D polynomials it levels off just above it.",
    "Bias is flat past the threshold; variance spikes at p = n and then collapses.",
    "Which interpolant the solver picks (set by the feature scaling) decides how well an interpolating model generalises."
